WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:06.700
The man himself, Baba Ramdev!

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:11.800
Not too long ago Baba Ramdev might have been
the most televised person in the world.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.460
In 2016 you could see his face on Indian TV channels

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:19.160
for an average of nineteen and a half hours every day.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:23.140
He’s a penniless yoga guru but his messages
aren’t all spiritual.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.940
You can see him applying face cream onto politicians,

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.620
gulping coconut oil in front of 
a thousands-strong crowd

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:33.960
or explaining on stage why you should clean
your floor with cow urine.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:39.760
A little bit weird?

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.120
Yes, at first.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.520
But in fact it’s ingenious.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:46.720
This is free advertising for his brainchild
Patanjali,

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.970
a 'Made in India' brand now selling everything

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:51.050
from cooking oil through hair loss products

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.000
to diapers and candles.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.800
Here is how a local herbal remedy business

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.380
grew into a consumer goods empire,

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:01.420
leaving multinational corporations 
scrambling in its wake.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:05.120
All thanks to this one godman turned businessman...

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:15.240
Godmen are so-called spiritual leaders that
mediate between God and man.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.760
This is fairly common in India and

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.960
these guys are almost treated and respected like God.

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:28.460
Some become really huge organizations and

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:31.600
people sometimes believe them really blindly.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:36.400
These guys wield enormous influence and power.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:41.360
But like many other godmen, for Ramdev this
path to power had humble beginnings.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.480
In the mid ‘90s he renounced all material possessions

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.440
and moved to Haridwar, a holy city on the Ganges, 
to teach yoga.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:53.020
There he was also managing an ashram, 
a type of religious community,

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:55.860
with his school friend Acharya Balkrishna.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:00.060
Together they were running a pharmacy where
they were selling homemade herbal remedies

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:03.520
based on the ancient Hindu system of medicine
called Ayurveda.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:08.539
This was when yoga was gaining 
popularity in the West.

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:11.000
Yoga will change your life, that’s all I’m saying.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:16.040
But in India it was still associated with
ancient texts and rigorous studies.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.760
Ramdev wanted to democratise it.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:22.200
He simplified the poses and was running free workshops,

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.620
showing that everyone could do it.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.100
He was also promoting yoga as a treatment
for many ailments.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.980
Obesity, infertility, depression…

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:32.340
even breast cancer,

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.820
his yoga had you covered.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.840
In 2002 Ramdev’s yoga camps started being
broadcast on TV.

00:02:38.849 --> 00:02:40.870
Despite airing in the early morning hours,

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:45.040
Ramdev’s signature 'belly roll' and
his playfulness made him an instant hit.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:50.820
But Ramdev and Balkrishna had a vision that
went beyond medicines and yoga,

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:53.360
they wanted to reach every Indian household

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:59.960
and in 2006 they set up Patanjali, with Balkrishna
owning more than 98% of the company.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:06.140
Patanjali started selling juices, grains and
beauty products, all based on natural ingredients.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:10.740
In the very early years you could hardly see
any marketing by the brand.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:13.260
All you could see was the products on the shelves.

00:03:13.269 --> 00:03:18.170
Baba Ramdev is actually the brand and the
power behind the brand

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:20.360
and without him the brand would be very little.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:26.160
But a lot of people who may not necessarily
be his followers use a lot of his products

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:32.320
because they believe that they are less contaminated
than other products available in the market.

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:39.340
Between 2011 and 2014 the number of Patanjali’s
products increased from 50 to 500.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:43.460
They started very small and launched a few products

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:47.800
and then it started catching fire in terms of popularity.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:53.920
I think it coincided with a sort of a rekindling
of nationalism in India

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:58.920
and a lot of Indians started identifying with
this company that was homegrown

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:02.120
and used very ancient Indian recipes

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:07.140
to make things like soaps, shampoos 
and even food products.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:12.820
Ramdev tapped into consumer patriotism and
became a symbol of India’s economic independence.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.660
This turned out to be a great sales pitch.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:31.360
Ramdev’s popularity was growing, 
and so was his influence.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:37.900
Having previously flirted with politics, Ramdev
started campaigning alongside right-wing politicians.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:42.980
In 2014 he mobilzed his followers to vote
for Narendra Modi for Prime Minister.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.560
When Modi won, Ramdev gained powerful allies.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:50.100
According to an investigation by Reuters,

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:54.680
Patanjali received more than 46 million dollars in
discounts on land deals

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:57.280
in states controlled by Modi’s party.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:01.300
Both Ramdev and Balkrishna claim they’re
not earning any salary.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.860
Their employees are told to accept lower pay
and treat their labour as a form of 'seva',

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:09.640
a spiritual practice of selfless service to
the community.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:14.860
All that helps Patanjali price its goods up
to 10% lower than its competition.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:18.840
India is a market of 1.3 billion people,

00:05:18.849 --> 00:05:23.699
a huge section of this population is at the
lower end of the pyramid

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:27.320
where they look for value for money, mass products.

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:32.540
So Patanjali kept doubling and tripling its revenues

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:37.620
and around 2016 - 2017 it was a huge competitor

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:44.000
for the largest multinationals operating out
of India, including Unilever and Procter &amp; Gamble.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:48.040
And all of these companies had to re-strategize

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:51.720
and also introduce herbal products like 
herbal toothpaste,

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:58.260
herbal soaps and shampoos so that they could compete with Baba Ramdev's Patanjali.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:01.940
Yet Patanjali has had its fair share of controversies;

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:04.400
noodles with dangerous ash content,

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:06.680
gooseberry juice failing lab tests,

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:09.180
legal actions over misleading ads.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:10.800
Ramdev’s reply?

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.220
It’s a foreign conspiracy!

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:20.740
Despite the controversies, in 2017 Patanjali’s revenue surpassed a billion dollars,

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:23.000
making Balkrishna a billionaire

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.840
while Ramdev was gloating.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:29.360
Baba Ramdev has good reason to smile, 
Patanjali Ayurved is growing at a gallop.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:41.500
Two years later that hasn’t happened, rather
the opposite, revenue has fallen.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:44.780
But Baba Ramdev’s ambition is increasingly
far-reaching.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:57.040
Ramdev’s vision of India - independent of
foreign influence -

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:00.700
seems to be attractive to an increasingly
nationalistic country.

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:04.060
But he’s still a highly controversial figure.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:10.060
In India there’s 1.3 billion people and
he certainly does not have 1.3 billion followers.

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:14.780
His charisma and his influence is balanced 
by the fact that

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:19.060
a lot of his rivals are the largest global
corporations in the world.

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:24.000
So I wouldn't think that he would get a pass
every time because he is a godman.

